{"shortDescription":"Vancouver, British Columbia--(Newsfile Corp. - September 21, 2026) - Southern Silver Exploration Corp. TSXV:SSV (the \"Company\" or \"Southern Silver\") reports assays from the first five holes of the definition drill program on the Puro Corazon target which provide better resolution to the distributio…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Vancouver, British Columbia--(Newsfile Corp. - September 21, 2026) - ",{"type":"b","children":["Southern Silver Exploration Corp."]}," ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSXV:SSV","text":"TSXV:SSV"}}," (the \"Company\" or \"Southern Silver\") reports assays from the first five holes of the definition drill program on the Puro Corazon target which provide better resolution to the distribution of the strongly silver enriched polymetallic mineralization."]},{"type":"p","children":["Highlight assays include:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["a ",{"type":"b","children":["35.0 metre"]}," interval averaging ",{"type":"b","children":["188g/t Ag"]},", 0.3%g/t Cu, ",{"type":"b","children":["4.9% Pb"]}," and ",{"type":"b","children":["4.6% Zn (399g/t AgEq)"]},", including a ",{"type":"b","children":["9.4 metre interval"]}," averaging ",{"type":"b","children":["344g/t Ag"]},", 0.2% Cu, ",{"type":"b","children":["9.1% Pb"]}," and ",{"type":"b","children":["6.7% Zn"]}," ",{"type":"b","children":["(665g/t AgEq)"]},"(1) from drillhole ",{"type":"b","children":["26CLM-225"]},";"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["a ",{"type":"b","children":["5.2 metre interval"]}," averaging ",{"type":"b","children":["277g/t Ag"]},", 0.1% Cu, ",{"type":"b","children":["9.9% Pb"]}," and ",{"type":"b","children":["6.3% Zn (598g/t AgEq)"]},", including a ",{"type":"b","children":["3.6 metre"]}," ",{"type":"b","children":["interval "]},"averaging ",{"type":"b","children":["384g/t Ag"]},", 0.1% Cu, ",{"type":"b","children":["13.4% Pb"]}," and",{"type":"b","children":[" 8.3% Zn (812g/t AgEq)"]},"(1) from drillhole ",{"type":"b","children":["26CLM-226"]},"; and"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["a ",{"type":"b","children":["5.3 metre interval"]}," averaging ",{"type":"b","children":["493g/t Ag"]},", 0.3% Cu, ",{"type":"b","children":["10.2% Pb"]}," and ",{"type":"b","children":["7.2% Zn (850g/t AgEq) from drillhole 26CLM-227"]},"."]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["(1) see AgEq calculation criteria in notes to Table 1. Intervals are reported as estimated true thickness unless otherwise indicated"]},{"type":"p","children":["These initial results are from the ongoing 14,000 metre core hole drill program that was started in June '26 and is designed to upgrade resource classification in the Puro Corazon target. The current drill program will test an area that is roughly a 200 metres strike-length by 300 metres down dip within the Puro Corazon claim. The above reported drill holes successfully targeted the upper part of the zone with nominal 40 metre step-outs from previously reported intercepts that include ",{"type":"b","children":["10.5 metres averaging 1,115g/t AgEq"]}," (see News Release dated December 1, 2025) from 25CLM-203 and ",{"type":"b","children":["10.4 metres averaging 743g/t AgEq"]}," (see News Release dated January 6, 2026) from 25CLM-205 as well as other mineralized intercepts."]},{"type":"p","children":["Both skarn and replacement styles of mineralization are identified in these holes with several intercepts, located well outboard of the Skarn zone, correlating with previous identified mineralization in the El Sol structural zone and the main skarn target."]},{"type":"p","children":["Vice President of Exploration, Rob Macdonald, stated, \"",{"type":"i","children":["This is a very solid start to the definition drill program on the Cerro Las Minitas project. These initial step out holes not only help confirm the previously reported thicknesses and grades of mineralization in this target area, but provide better definition as to the projection of several of the mineralized zones. Drilling continues on the project and the Company anticipates good news flow over the coming weeks and months.\""]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The Company reports that drilling continues with eight of 30 planned holes having been completed to date with one hole in progress. Logging and sampling continue and assays from three holes are pending."]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:8fb4c8622094b-c0141b6f8d38f7ade5e53c10437327ed","source-width":996,"source-height":717,"bg-color":"#cad4d4"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Figure 1: Plan view of the drilling on the recently acquired Puro Corazon Claim."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["To view an enhanced version of this graphic, please visit:"]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:8fb4c8622094b-c0141b6f8d38f7ade5e53c10437327ed","source-width":996,"source-height":717,"bg-color":"#cad4d4"}}},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:8fb4c8622094b-38b52680d8214a2bf342d59109a276f7","source-width":893,"source-height":1041,"bg-color":"#e1e2ee"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Figure 2: Longitudinal Section of the Puro Corazon Target, looking east. Note: pierce points reflect intercepts into the main Skarn zone"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["To view an enhanced version of this graphic, please visit:"]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:8fb4c8622094b-38b52680d8214a2bf342d59109a276f7","source-width":893,"source-height":1041,"bg-color":"#e1e2ee"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Next Steps"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Work continues to incorporate results from the earlier 2025-26 Puro Corazon drilling into the larger Cerro Las Minitas project which is expected to enhance the project economics and the scalability of the mine plan. Work continues advancing numerous upside opportunities identified su